1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,853
On this air traffic control desk you can see two airplanes flying at the same altitude, on perpendicular routes that cross at point O.

2
00:00:08,803 --> 00:00:14,946
One is two hundred and twenty-five miles from O and flies at four hundred and fifty miles per hour.

3
00:00:14,946 --> 00:00:19,335
The other is three hundred miles away and flies at six hundred.

4
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:25,585
Play the clock or move the time to see how they approach each other, and adjust the clock speed if you need to.

5
00:00:25,585 --> 00:00:32,712
On the graph of the distance between the airplanes, the slope of the tangent is the rate at which that distance changes.

6
00:00:32,712 --> 00:00:39,840
With Go to the instant you place yourself at the moment of the problem, and with Reveal answer you check your calculation.

7
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:45,226
If you keep moving time forward, you will see what happens when both reach point O.

